{
  "note": "Which links in a story get a preview card (src/lib/links/storyLinks.ts; read by storyLinks.test.ts and StoryMarkdown.test.tsx on the web, and by the apps' story parsers). A paragraph whose only meaningful child is an http(s) link ([t](url), <url>, a reference link; no picture inside) or a run of plain text that is exactly one link is a standalone link, keyed by its normalized URL. `soleLinks`: every such paragraph's key, in reading order (duplicates and our own hosts included) — what a parser must find. `links`: what the server unfurls and stores — soleLinks without our own hosts and bare IP addresses, each once, at most 10. `inline`: links in the story that must stay inline, even if a preview for them existed. `webDrawsNone`: the web renders no paragraph there (a tight list), so it draws no card, as with card embeds.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "bare-https",
      "markdown": "雨停了。\n\nhttps://example.com/rain\n\n我出門散步。",
      "soleLinks": ["https://example.com/rain"],
      "links": ["https://example.com/rain"]
    },
    {
      "id": "bare-www",
      "markdown": "www.example.org/notes",
      "soleLinks": ["https://www.example.org/notes"],
      "links": ["https://www.example.org/notes"]
    },
